From 4bef7feafd3ef64625ae42e4cbb82232b9e9e997 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <claude@anthropic.com>
Date: Thu, 20 Aug 2026 00:02:51 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Migrate backend to run on Vercel serverless while keeping
 Railway working unchanged

- Replace in-memory workflow state + WebSocket push with a DB-backed
  Workflow table, advanced one stage per POST /workflow/{id}/advance
  call. Fixes: in-memory state and BackgroundTasks continuation don't
  survive across Vercel's isolated, short-lived function instances.
- PDFGenerator now builds entirely in memory (BytesIO) instead of
  writing to local disk -- Vercel's filesystem is read-only outside
  /tmp, which doesn't persist across invocations anyway.
- SQLAlchemy connection pooling is now env-aware: NullPool on Vercel
  (detected via the VERCEL env var Vercel sets automatically) so
  Supabase's PgBouncer does the real pooling; unchanged QueuePool
  behavior on Railway.
- Added GET /health.
- Trimmed requirements.txt from 137 to 19 packages -- removed
  streamlit, langchain/langgraph/langsmith, pandas/pyarrow/plotly/
  pydeck/altair, boto3/botocore, redis, watchdog, and their
  transitive deps, none of which are imported anywhere in the live
  FastAPI app (verified by grepping every import in src/, api/,
  database/, not assumed). Matters for Vercel's function bundle size
  limit.
- Added vercel.json + .vercelignore.
- /ws/workflow/{id} kept in place for Railway (still works there);
  it's simply unreachable on Vercel, which the frontend no longer
  depends on for progress anyway.
